@startuml state_tmpfs_file_lifecycle
!include ../../../design/theme.iuml

title tmpfs File Lifecycle (ADR-0037)

[*] --> Created : plugin registers with\nscope.ScopeTelemetry

Created --> Writing : first serialized TelemetryOperation\nprotobuf written by drain worker

Writing --> Notified : plugin poll observes\nreadable range {offset, len}\nvia socket

Notified --> Reading : plugin wakes,\nstarts pread at offset

Reading --> Acked : plugin finishes read,\nsends TelemetryAck{len}

Acked --> Truncated : server truncates\nconsumed bytes\n(ftruncate / advance)

Truncated --> Writing : next whole operation\nserialized and written

Writing --> CeilingReached : file size >= 15M\nbefore plugin acks

CeilingReached --> ForcedFlush : server exposes\nreadable range immediately

ForcedFlush --> Reading : plugin reads\nbefore more data arrives

state "Overflow handling" as overflow {
  CeilingReached : increment TelemetryOverflowDropped
  CeilingReached : truncate oldest unconsumed data
  CeilingReached : emit gap notification via socket
}

Created --> Closed : plugin disconnects
Acked --> Closed : plugin disconnects
Writing --> Closed : server shutdown
Closed --> [*] : unlink /dev/shm file

note right of CeilingReached
  Overflow is bounded and counted.
  Oldest unconsumed data is truncated
  first (FIFO loss). A gap counter
  replaces ADR-0036's SkippedOperations
  for the tmpfs path.
end note

note left of Truncated
  Truncation advances a read offset;
  the file is not physically resized
  every cycle. Periodic ftruncate
  compacts the file.
end note

@enduml
